<?php
function cm_render_how_to() {
    $questions = [
        [ __( 'How do I set up the volunteer account page?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Create a WordPress page, add [fxm-account] in a Shortcode block, and publish it. Select that page as the Account Page in WP Charity Settings → Dashboard and save. Visitors can sign up or log in there; signed-in volunteers can manage their campaigns and profile.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I create a campaign and accept donations?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Create a campaign in the WordPress dashboard. Add its title, story, image and fundraising goal, then select a WooCommerce donation product in the campaign settings. Publish the campaign. WooCommerce handles checkout and the payment methods enabled in your store.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I offer different donation amounts?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Use a simple WooCommerce product for one amount or a variable product for a choice of amounts. Set up the product prices and variations in WooCommerce, then select that product for the campaign. Custom amounts require a compatible Name Your Price setup; they are not provided by this plugin alone.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How can volunteers raise money for a campaign?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Enable volunteer campaigns on the main campaign. Volunteers can sign in to their account, choose New Campaign, select the main campaign, and add their own story. Their campaign uses the main campaign’s donation product.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'Why is a volunteer campaign still a draft?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'The Volunteer Campaign Status setting controls approval. With Draft selected, an administrator must publish the campaign before it becomes public. Published allows automatic approval. Volunteers receive an email when a draft is submitted and when it is approved.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I remind an administrator to review my campaign?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Open My Campaigns in your account and choose Remind admin to review next to a draft. This sends the review notification again. It does not publish the campaign.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do fundraising goals work?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Set a donation goal in the campaign details. A positive goal displays progress toward that amount. Selecting a main campaign in the volunteer form can fill in its goal and dates. Reaching a goal displays a thank-you message; it does not automatically stop donations. In either campaign editor, enable "Hide goal progress once the target is reached" to hide the target, percentage, progress bar and thank-you message once the goal is met. The amount raised and donation controls remain visible. If the total falls below the goal again, progress reappears.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I add a picture or video?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Upload a campaign image and, if wanted, enter a YouTube video link. A 1200 × 630 image is recommended. You can edit these details later through My Campaigns. Your profile picture is changed separately in Profile.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I share or edit my campaign?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Open My Campaigns and use Edit, View Campaign or Share Campaign. Share opens your browser’s sharing feature. You can also copy the campaign page address. Only published campaigns are visible to other visitors.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'Where can I see donations?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Volunteers can open Donations in their account to see donations to their own campaigns, including donor contact details. Administrators can use Reports for donation lines or Help for campaign summaries. Use Next and Previous to browse more results; View orders opens a campaign’s orders.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'Why can totals differ between screens?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Help and the public progress display count the full value of each matching order once for that campaign. The campaign list, Reports and account Donations use only the matching donation lines. The campaign list also includes published and draft volunteer campaigns directly beneath a main campaign when volunteers are enabled. These differences matter when an order contains other purchases or donations to more than one campaign.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'Which orders appear in donation totals?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Completed, Processing and On hold orders are included. Pending payment, Failed, Cancelled and Refunded orders are excluded. Partial refunds are not separately deducted from the stored amounts shown by these reports.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I download donations for my records?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'In Reports, choose Export full report as CSV to download every donation line. In Help, choose Export CSV next to a campaign to download its matching orders using full order amounts. Downloads include all results, not only the current page.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I correct a donation assigned to the wrong campaign?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'An administrator can open the WooCommerce order and use Donation campaign to select the correct campaign for an order line. Check the campaign name and ID before choosing Assign or Reassign. This changes the campaign association, not the payment or the product purchased.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I update my details or reset my password?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Sign in and open Profile to change your name, email, biography, picture or password. Leave both password fields empty to keep your password. If you cannot log in, choose Forgot Password and follow the link sent to your email address.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'How do I choose who receives campaign notifications?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'In Dashboard, enter notification email addresses separated by commas for new campaign review notices. If left empty, the site administrator’s email is used. Donation notices go automatically to the author of each campaign using their account email address; you do not need to add authors to WooCommerce’s recipient list. Optional integration URLs can send registration or approval information to your connected service.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'Will I receive an email when someone donates?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Yes. When an order enters Processing, Completed or On hold, a notification is queued for each campaign author. It includes the donor’s name, order number, status and donation amounts for your own campaigns. On hold means payment is awaiting confirmation. Several donations to your campaigns in the same order are grouped into one email. Later status changes do not send it again. Volunteer donations notify the volunteer campaign’s author, not the main campaign’s author. Existing orders are not emailed in bulk when the plugin is updated.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
        [ __( 'What if a donation notification does not arrive?', 'wp-charity' ), __( 'Check your account email address and spam folder. Notifications are sent in the background, so they may take a little time. If the email service rejects a message, the plugin retries up to three times, five minutes apart. Administrators can check WooCommerce’s Scheduled Actions and wp-charity logs. After correcting a delivery problem, use Retry failed campaign author notifications in the order’s Order actions. Authors whose messages were already accepted by the email service are not sent another copy.', 'wp-charity' ) ],
    ];
    echo '<h2>' . esc_html__( 'How To', 'wp-charity' ) . '</h2><p>' . esc_html__( 'Answers for setting up campaigns and helping your volunteers.', 'wp-charity' ) . '</p><div class="cm-how-to">';
    foreach ( $questions as $question ) {
        echo '<details><summary>' . esc_html( $question[0] ) . '</summary><p>' . esc_html( $question[1] ) . '</p></details>';
    }
    echo '</div>';
}
